  "nl_text": "The database schema for the database named 'rschema_0446' consists of 9 tables. The database is used for managing various aspects of a farming system, including user management, sensor data collection, meteorological data, crop management, growth model creation, water and fertilizer supply, user operations, system performance evaluation, and model performance evaluation.\nThe 'user' table holds information about the users of the system, including their unique ID, username, password, phone number, registration time, last login time, and role. The primary key for this table is 'user_id'.\nThe 'sensor' table holds data collected by various sensors, including the time of data collection, soil moisture, temperature, rainfall, light intensity, sensor location, sensor burial depth, and a foreign key 'meteorological_id' referencing the 'meteorology' table. The primary key for this table is 'sensor_id'.\nThe 'meteorology' table holds meteorological data, including a unique ID, timestamp, temperature, humidity, rainfall, wind speed, light intensity, and location. The primary key for this table is 'meteorological_id'.\nThe 'crop' table holds information about the crops, including their unique ID, name, type, and a foreign key 'model_id' referencing the 'growth_model' table. The primary key for this table is 'crop_id'.\nThe 'growth_model' table holds information about the growth models, including their unique ID, schema name, model parameters, and model creation time. The primary key for this table is 'model_id'.\nThe 'user_water_and_fertilizer_supply' table holds information about water and fertilizer supplies, including the admin ID, crop type, supply time, supply location, water supply, fertilizer supply, and a foreign key 'associated_sensor_id' referencing the 'sensor' table. The primary key for this table is a composite key of 'admin_id' and 'associated_sensor_id'.\nThe 'user_operation' table holds information about user operations, including the admin ID, crop ID, operation time, operation type, operation location, and operation details. The primary key for this table is a composite key of 'crop_id' and 'admin_id'.\nThe 'system_performance_evaluation' and 'model_performance_evaluation' tables hold performance evaluations, including the admin ID, crop ID, evaluation time, evaluation metric name, evaluation metric value, and evaluation location. The primary keys for these tables are composite keys of 'crop_id' and 'admin_id' for 'system_performance_evaluation' and 'model_id' and 'crop_id' for 'model_performance_evaluation'.\nAll tables have foreign keys that reference other tables, ensuring referential integrity and maintaining the relationships between the tables. The DELETE and UPDATE rules are set to CASCADE, meaning that if a record in the referenced table is deleted or updated, the corresponding records in the referencing table will automatically be deleted or updated as well.",
  "gold_question": "Requirements:\n1.User Information: Each registered user has a unique username, password, phone number, registration time, last login time, and role. Users can supply water and fertilizer to crops through sensors, and the system needs to record the supply time, location, amount of water, and amount of fertilizer. Additionally, any other actions taken by the user on the crop (such as planting, fertilizing, etc.) need to be recorded, including the time, location, type, and details of the action. Users can also evaluate the crop’s growth performance through the system.\n2.Sensor Deployment: Sensors precisely measure meteorological data and record information such as the data collection time, soil moisture, temperature, rainfall, light intensity, sensor location, and burial depth. Each sensor can infer corresponding meteorological data.\n3.Meteorology: Each meteorological record includes timestamp, temperature, humidity, rainfall, wind speed, light intensity, and location.\n4.Crops: Each crop has a unique crop ID, name, type, and a matching growth model.\n5.Growth Model: Each crop has a corresponding growth model, which includes the model name, parameters, and creation time. The crop is evaluated using this model, and the evaluation records the name of the evaluation metric, its value, and the location of the evaluation.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_deepseek/0446.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0446\nCREATE TABLE `user` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(15) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `registration_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `last_login_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `role` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `meteorology` (\n  `meteorological_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `timestamp` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `temperature` float NOT NULL,\n  `humidity` float NOT NULL,\n  `rainfall` float NOT NULL,\n  `wind_speed` float NOT NULL,\n  `light_intensity` float NOT NULL,\n  `location` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`meteorological_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `sensor` (\n  `sensor_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `data_collection_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `soil_moisture` float NOT NULL,\n  `temperature` float NOT NULL,\n  `rainfall` float NOT NULL,\n  `light_intensity` float NOT NULL,\n  `sensor_location` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `sensor_burial_depth` float NOT NULL,\n  `meteorological_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`sensor_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `sensor_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`meteorological_id`) REFERENCES `meteorology` (`meteorological_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `growth_model` (\n  `model_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `schema_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `model_parameters` text NOT NULL,\n  `model_creation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`model_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `crop` (\n  `crop_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `type` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `model_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`crop_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `crop_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`model_id`) REFERENCES `growth_model` (`model_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user_water_and_fertilizer_supply` (\n  `admin_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `associated_sensor_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `crop_type` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `supply_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `supply_location` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `water_supply` float NOT NULL,\n  `fertilizer_supply` float NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`admin_id`, `associated_sensor_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `user_water_and_fertilizer_supply_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`associated_sensor_id`) REFERENCES `sensor` (`sensor_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user_operation` (\n  `admin_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `crop_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `operation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `operation_type` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `operation_location` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `operation_details` text NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`crop_id`, `admin_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `user_operation_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`crop_id`) REFERENCES `crop` (`crop_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `system_performance_evaluation` (\n  `admin_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `crop_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `evaluation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `evaluation_metric_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `evaluation_metric_value` float NOT NULL,\n  `evaluation_location` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`crop_id`, `admin_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `system_performance_evaluation_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`crop_id`) REFERENCES `crop` (`crop_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `model_performance_evaluation` (\n  `model_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `crop_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `evaluation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `evaluation_metric_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `evaluation_metric_value` float NOT NULL,\n  `evaluation_location` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`model_id`, `crop_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `model_performance_evaluation_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`crop_id`) REFERENCES `crop` (`crop_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `model_performance_evaluation_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`model_id`) REFERENCES `growth_model` (`model_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
